t Greg Abbott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas governor pits three-term incumbent Greg Abbott against state Representative Gina Hinojosa, with a Libertarian also on the ballot. Recent polls from late October consistently show Abbott ahead, with margins ranging from about two to five points, though a couple of registered-voter surveys put the race within one. Averages across aggregators land near a three-point Abbott lead. Prediction markets price Hinojosa's chances in the mid-to-high thirties.\n\nAbbott holds a commanding financial advantage, with roughly $67 million on hand after outraising Hinojosa throughout the race, though both posted their biggest hauls in the final stretch. Ratings from nonpartisan analysts cluster at Lean R, with one Tilt R and one Tossup. The race is competitive by Texas standards but the incumbent remains favored heading into Election Day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1819, "margin": -4.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2894, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2702, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -3.3}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2978, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2717, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2616, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2625, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2248, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2304, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2288, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.255, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2522, "margin": -3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2859, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3188, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3088, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2554, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-